.TH COZY 1 "November 2026" "cozy" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cozy \- a small functional matrix language for econometrics
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cozy
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ file.cz " ...]"
.br
.B cozy-workbench
.RI [ port ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cozy
is an interpreter for Cozy, a functional language with first-class
matrices, exact automatic differentiation (dual and hyper-dual
numbers), sparse matrices, calendar dates, missing-value handling, and
professional linear-algebra and optimization backends (LAPACK via
OpenBLAS or Accelerate; NLopt) behind build-time seams.
.PP
With no arguments it starts an interactive REPL. With file arguments it
runs each script in order and exits; the exit code is nonzero if any
script raises an error, so scripts compose with
.BR make (1)
and shell pipelines. Runtime errors name the full closure call chain.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-workbench [port]
Serve the browser workbench (editor, plots pane, documentation tabs) on
localhost at the given port (default 8765). The
.B cozy-workbench
command does this and opens the browser.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version, linear-algebra backend, optimization backend, and
build date.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print a usage summary.
.TP
.B \-\-tokens, \-\-ast, \-\-dis
Compiler introspection: read a program on stdin and print its token
stream, syntax tree, or bytecode disassembly.
.TP
.B \-\-sample
Print a sample session.
.SH THE LANGUAGE, BRIEFLY
.nf
cozy> let A = rand(3); A \\ ones(3, 1)
cozy> let f = fn x, tol = 1e-8 -> x^2 - 2
cozy> minimize[b = [0.0; 0.0]] ssr(b)
cozy> load("ts"); mean(growth(t.gdp), "omit")
.fi
.PP
Type
.B help
in the REPL for a tour,
.B help(name)
for any builtin with executable examples, and
.B manual
to read the full manual. Every transcript in the manual and the
accompanying book re-executes at every release; the documentation
cannot go stale.
.SH PACKAGES
.B load("name")
resolves bare names through the
.I packages/
directory of the development tree, each colon-separated directory in
.BR COZY_PATH ,
the directory of the running binary, and the installed
.IR share/cozy ;
a miss names every place searched.
.B packeur
is an interactive package picker. Installed packages include
.BR dist ", " optim ", " ts ", " finance ", " sparselin ", "
.BR autodiff ", and " symb .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B COZY_PATH
Colon-separated extra directories searched by
.BR load() .
.TP
.B COZY_PLOT_TERM
Plot backend override: an empty value uses gnuplot when present;
.B ascii
renders text plots;
.B svg
writes SVG files (the workbench shows them in its plots pane).
.TP
.B COZY_PLOT_OUT
Output file for gnuplot terminals that write files.
.TP
.B OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS
Caps OpenBLAS threading; 2 is often best for interactive-sized
problems on hybrid-core laptops.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/cozy/packages
Installed packages.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/cozy/docs
The browser workbench and its bundled documentation.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/cozy/data
Sample data sets used by the book's worked problems.
.SH BUILDING
.B make
builds the zero-dependency tier0 interpreter.
.B make BACKEND=openblas OPTIM=nlopt
(Linux) or
.B make BACKEND=accelerate OPTIM=nlopt
(macOS) links the professional backends.
.B make install
installs into
.I ~/.local
(override with
.BR PREFIX= ).
.B buildinfo()
in the REPL reports what the running binary was built with.
.SH SEE ALSO
The manual, the package guide, and the book of worked econometrics
problems: in the REPL as
.BR manual ", " "manual packages" ", and " "manual book" ;
as PDFs in the source tree; and in the browser workbench.
.SH AUTHOR
Mico Mrkaic, with the methodology and releases engineered in
collaboration with Claude (Anthropic).
